
# 🚚 FMCG Supply Chain OTIF Dashboard – AtliQ Mart

## 📄 Project Description

This Power BI dashboard was developed for **AtliQ Mart**, an emerging FMCG company based in Gujarat, to help resolve customer service issues caused by delayed or incomplete deliveries. The goal was to provide visibility into **On-Time**, **In-Full**, and **OTIF (On-Time-In-Full)** delivery metrics to improve service levels and ensure customer satisfaction before expanding into new cities.

---

## ❓ Problem Statement

AtliQ Mart has been losing key customers due to delivery-related service issues. There was no reliable system in place to monitor delivery performance metrics on a day-to-day basis. The **Supply Chain team** required a data-driven dashboard to:
- Track daily service levels for each customer.
- Analyze trends in On-Time, In-Full, and OTIF delivery percentages.
- Take swift action where targets are not being met.

The task was to design and deliver a dashboard solution using inputs from the stakeholder meeting and supporting documentation.

---

## 📊 Key Features & Insights

- 📦 Daily OT%, IF%, and OTIF% tracking for all customers  
- 🎯 Comparison of actual performance vs customer-specific targets  
- 🗺️ City-wise and Product-wise breakdown of delivery issues  
- 📅 Time-series analysis to detect recurring delivery problems    

---

## 🔧 Tools & Techniques Used

- **Power BI Desktop** for building interactive dashboards  
- **Power Query** for data transformation and relationship setup  
- **DAX** for calculating OT%, IF%, and OTIF% metrics  
- **Conditional formatting** to highlight deviations from targets  
- **Time intelligence** for comparing performance over time

---

## 📁 Dataset Information

- **Key Tables:**
  - `Customer Orders`: Daily order data including planned and actual delivery dates and quantities.  
  - `Customer Targets`: Target OTIF% and service level goals for each customer.  
  - `Product`: Information about product categories and SKUs.  
  - `City`: Regional dimension to analyze location-based performance.  
  - `Date`: Calendar table for time-based filtering and aggregation.

---

## 🧮 Sample DAX Measures

- `OT % = DIVIDE(OnTimeOrders, TotalOrders)`  
- `IF % = DIVIDE(InFullOrders, TotalOrders)`  
- `OTIF % = DIVIDE(OTIFOrders, TotalOrders)`  
- `OTIF Gap = [OTIF %] - [Target OTIF %]`

